{
 "format": "qpp-workbook",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "Pulling wires taut",
 "description": "In Picturing Quantum Processes wires are pieces of string: only what connects to what matters. Pull a diagram taut and every snake straightens, needless crossings undo, and each box riding a wire slides along it — coming out transposed if it went round a bend. Every proof step here was made by “⟿ Taut step” and is checked equal to the one before. On the right is a tangle to try yourself: press T (or ⟿) to watch it pull taut, scrub back and forth, then Apply.",
 "summary": {
  "circuits": 0,
  "diagrams": 1,
  "proofs": 5
 },
